WEBVTT

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:19.420
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:19.420
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:19.420
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:46.150
Silver-White Valley

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:46.150
Chapter 2

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:54.130
Planet Kapche-Lanka is located 8.6 light
years in the Free Planets Alliance direction...

00:01:54.130 --> 00:02:00.750
...from the critical strategic point of
the Imperial Force, Iserlohn Fortress.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:06.490
Out of the 688 days of its solar cycle,
more than 608 days are wintry...

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:09.310
...and blizzards occur
almost every day.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.960
Because of this, it isn't suitable
to use aircraft in combat;

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.560
...therefore, battles mostly
take place on the ground.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:19.780
We'll do our final checks.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:20.990
Go ahead.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.360
Main gun, 120 mm rail cannon.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.700
120 mm rail cannon, normal.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.330
Sub-gun, all-purpose charged
particle beam cannon.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.000
All-purpose charged particle
beam cannon, normal.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.650
Vehicle body-strength
self-diagnosis system.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.040
Vehicle body-strength
self-diagnosis system, normal.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:43.720
Radio wave
absorption system.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:46.410
Radio wave absorption
system, normal.

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.480
Infrared ray
absorption system.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.290
Infrared ray absorption
system, normal.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.560
Low-frequency
absorption system.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:59.100
Low-frequency absorption
system, normal.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:01.150
Hydrogen battery,
residual quantity.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:05.240
Hydrogen battery,
residual quantity, 99.8%.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.060
Okay, next.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.850
Control navigation system.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.960
Control navigation system, normal.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.170
Noctovision.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.780
Noctovision, normal.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.070
Directional sound
analysis system.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.240
Directional sound
analysis system, normal.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:07.200
The rebel ground troops who presumptuously
call themselves "The Free Planets Alliance"...

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.400
...are suspected of constructing
a base in a mountainous region...

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.730
...roughly 600 to 700 km
northwest of this base.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:20.200
Your mission is to gather the information
necessary to ascertain its location...

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:25.400
...so that our troops may attack
and destroy or seize it.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:27.900
That is all.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:34.210
What is the
Captain trying to do ?

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:40.260
This briefing right before departure and the
orders that, as always, lack anything concrete.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:44.510
It doesn't seem like he wants
this mission to succeed.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.040
No.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:48.660
Moreover, he clearly
has malicious intent.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.140
But the reason
isn't quite clear.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.800
For simple harassment,
he seems to be going too far.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.780
Whatever the case, the Captain
may be hoping for our failure...

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.450
...but we aren't obligated
to fulfill his expectations.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:07.950
We'll just humble him.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:12.540
Then shall we seize the
enemy base by ourselves ?

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:19.120
That's right.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.650
That's the spirit, Kircheis.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:18.490
How did it go ?

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:20.750
Without a hitch.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:22.220
Good.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.200
I can do the driving.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:33.120
We'll switch at
some point anyway.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:36.530
Or don't you feel
safe with me driving ?

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:42.400
I know all too well that you were at the top when it came to practical training as well.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:46.120
I couldn't beat you in
a few areas, though...

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:50.180
...marksmanship, hand-to-hand
combat, driving skills, too.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:54.490
That way, I can become
your chauffeur anytime.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:58.080
In the future, there'll be no
shortage of chauffeurs for me.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.650
The same goes for bodyguards.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.810
But your job will be
much more than that.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:07.180
In my place, you'll have to lead
a fleet of thousands of ships.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.150
The important thing
is strategy, you mean ?

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:12.750
That's right.

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:16.440
Of course, grades in school
aren't a good indicator.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:21.120
They focus too much on memorization and
imitation, and don't foster imagination.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:26.360
What you find important are imaginative
and conceptual capabilities, right ?

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:27.560
That's right.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:33.280
But really, those in that base have no
sense whatsoever of strategic importance.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:36.930
No, it's not just those
people in that base.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:40.110
The same goes for the
brass of the Imperial Force.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:44.150
They aren't thinking at all about why we fight and what we must do to accomplish our objective.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:50.550
They only think about fighting the enemy that's there and they think winning those battles is good enough.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:52.050
You're right.

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:54.900
This armored vehicle
is a good example.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:00.660
Such an expensive machine,
with state-of-the-art electronics...

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:03.550
...but soon, there'll be something
else developed to counter them.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:06.100
Each side neutralizes the other
side's technology, and as a result...

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:11.000
...we still use military
dogs and carrier pigeons.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.620
In that sense, our enemy,
the Alliance Force, is in the same boat.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:15.380
Yes.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.690
Neither of them can escape
their ossified ways of thinking...

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:21.450
...and they merely keep
repeating meaningless scuffles.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:27.660
If that has to be the case, let's hope
the enemy has some talented people.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:31.710
Otherwise, they won't be
worth fighting against.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:39.000
In the 482 years after the
establishment of the Galactic Empire...

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:45.310
...by Rudolph von Goldenbaum's usurpation, which took place after the Galactic Federation era...

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:51.100
...people who escaped from the Empire's
oppression founded the Free Planets Alliance.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:54.960
The two firmly opposed one another,
and 150 years have passed since then.

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:00.680
This planet, Kapche-Lanka,
was one of the conflict areas.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.720
Despite being blessed with an
abundance of natural resources...

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:08.050
...this planet wasn't exactly
indispensable to either side.

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:11.750
But because of a lowly reason - 
"We don't want to give it up to the other"...

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:15.140
...fierce battles were
continuously waged every year.

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:18.890
We're past the 500km mark.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:20.900
Roger.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:23.920
It's gotten dark.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:27.120
Should we switch
to noctovision ?

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:28.840
Yes.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:31.680
What's wrong ?

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:32.920
This is strange.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.330
Please take a look.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.170
Let's check it out.

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.530
Stop the vehicle.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:42.260
Right.

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:51.200
It's not a malfunction
of the warning lamp.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:53.600
The hydrogen battery has
actually been consumed.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:57.820
We replaced the hydrogen
battery with a new one.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.310
I confirmed it
with my own eyes.

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:00.210
Yes.

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:01.490
I confirmed it, too.

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:07.500
But it's not like we stayed with the
vehicle continuously after we checked it.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:19.280
I guess that means
it's the Captain's doing.

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:23.150
But this goes further
than mere punishment.

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:24.880
He wants us to
die here, I guess.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:29.980
But for what reason has
he gone so far to plot this ?

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.690
He can't just say that it
was a joke after the fact.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.830
I want to know that, too.

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:43.730
What should we
do, Lord Reinhard ?

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:47.170
If we try to go back,
we'll run out of fuel.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:49.990
In any case,
let's spend the night.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.690
Even if we want
to move, we can't.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:54.200
Sure.

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:59.060
Then let's drive into that lower
ground and camouflage the vehicle.

00:10:59.410 --> 00:10:59.960
Yeah.

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:00.600
Let's do that.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.700
I'll do the rest here.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.800
Kircheis, erase our tracks.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:25.370
Sure.

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:41.530
That's plenty.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:44.680
The snow will keep
falling and erase the rest.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:47.100
Right.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.400
I'll scatter sensors
around just to be safe.

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:07.850
It's completely dead.

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.400
What are we going to do about
monitoring the sensors we placed ?

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:15.150
We can do that with
a portable computer.

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:16.900
But we don't
have a heater.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:21.100
With the arctic clothes we have,
we probably won't die of cold.

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:23.100
But anyway,
I'm feeling hungry.

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.550
We can't cook the
nonperishable foods, either.

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:31.140
Among them, the rye bread is just about
the only thing we can eat without heating.

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:33.350
That's fine.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:37.000
Unless we eat something, we could
die of hunger instead of the cold.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:13:00.130
I want to eat one
of Sister's onion pies.

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:04.410
And a cup of hot
coffee, with lots of...

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:06.900
Cream...

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:06.900
...lots of it !

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:11.230
Lady Annerose's pie...

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:15.310
Reinhard !

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:16.540
Sieg !

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:19.100
Wash your hands
and come quick.

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:21.550
A hot-out-of-the-oven
pie is waiting for you.

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:34.600
But really.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:40.800
It's wrong to compare
it with my sister's pie...

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:42.770
...since this thing
is like cattle feed.

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:43.640
It's horrible.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:45.280
Right.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:48.590
Quality-wise, it doesn't seem to meet
the standards set by the military.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:53.640
That Captain may be routing goods
to the black market or something.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:54.940
That's possible.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:57.660
You can tell just by looking at the
degenerate ways of his soldiers.

00:13:57.660 --> 00:13:58.360
Right.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:02.410
When a society or organization goes
corrupt, it always starts from the top.

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:04.300
Once I return, I'll
reveal this by all means.

00:14:05.140 --> 00:14:06.910
Once you return, right ?

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:08.520
That's the issue.

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:13.880
At this rate, we have no way of going
back there, and we'll die of cold or hunger.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:17.840
Even if it's not death by cold or hunger,
I don't want to die on the ground.

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:23.070
Since I can't be immortal, I want to die
in a place appropriate for me, at least.

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:26.600
It's understandable.

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:31.990
His feet are not there
to walk on the ground...

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:34.530
...they're there for
him to fly in the sky.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:39.590
Kircheis, is there a place you'd
rather choose to die than this ?

00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:42.490
Whatever the case, you wouldn't want
to die in a place like this, would you ?

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:50.870
As long as you and Lady Annerose are
by my side, I don't need anything else.

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:56.960
It's no small wish.

00:14:56.960 --> 00:15:03.070
Right now, Lady Annerose is in
captivity - in that prison called Court.

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:07.550
The things I'm
going to grasp...

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:10.510
...no matter what they are,
half of them will be yours.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:14.400
Fame, power, treasure,
and everything else, too.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:22.000
But for now, it'll be just this horrible
black bread and lukewarm coffee.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.790
And hope, I guess.

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:26.090
For now,
that's plenty enough.

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:38.750
Once you drink your coffee,
go ahead and get some sleep.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:39.490
That's an order.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:41.530
Yes, Ensign.

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:18.250
Sieg.

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:23.600
Please take care of Reinhard.

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:28.960
He isn't trying
to make more friends...

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:33.170
...but I can understand why he
feels content with having just you.

00:16:34.690 --> 00:16:36.820
Would you please do that{i.e. take care of Reinhard} ?

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:37.430
Yes.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:38.390
Yes !

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.500
Even in exchange for my life.

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:42.230
That's not good.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:44.890
Both of you should
come home safe.

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:53.710
A friendship where one has to sacrifice
himself for the other won't last long.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:58.930
I want you both to be
indispensable to one another.

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:03.350
Please stay in a mutually
giving kind of friendship.

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:05.050
Yes.

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:07.380
I'll do as you say,
Lady Annerose.

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:18.210
Am I indispensable
to you, too ?

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:25.660
Someday, will I be able to become
someone you need more than anyone else ?

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:36.300
Lord Reinhard !

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:40.120
Three enemy vehicles
are loitering around.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.280
You took the trouble
to go outside and look ?

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:47.900
You should have woken me up.

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:50.110
I just woke you, didn't I ?

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:55.460
Since we aren't using any energy
here, they can't detect us.

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:59.600
It's a lucky accident, but we
have the advantage because of it.

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:05.060
Still, I didn't expect that the enemy
would be encroaching this far.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:08.620
Captain Herder probably
didn't anticipate that either.

00:18:09.220 --> 00:18:11.480
But he might
have hoped for it.

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:17.200
In any case, even though we're new to the region, he sent us to such a dangerous area alone.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:21.780
If something were to happen to us, won't it
become a problem for him at a later time ?

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:25.350
I'd imagine he has special
connections with the brass.

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:30.600
To someone who has the power
to cover up problems of this kind.

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:35.810
Then this a plot
by that "someone" ?

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:38.010
Most likely.

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:43.410
It seems to go beyond the matter
of the Captain's personal face-saving.

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:47.900
Even before our arrival on this planet, they
might have been preparing to welcome us.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:49.840
What are we going to do ?

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:54.000
If we seize one
of the enemy vehicles...

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:58.200
...our chances of getting back there
alive will increase significantly.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:18:59.690
Don't you agree ?

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:00.760
Yes.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:01.950
It'll multiply
by a few times.

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:03.980
All right.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:15.510
These are all the
weapons we have, right ?

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.390
We can probably use these.

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:01.540
One down.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:07.740
A smile of victory definitely
suits Lord Reinhard.

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:15.050
I'm sorry,
Reinhard, Sieg.

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:18.600
I've been told that His Majesty
has come down with a cold.

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:20.270
I have to go.

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:56.520
It was a missile attack !

00:21:57.350 --> 00:21:58.100
Let's spread out.

00:21:58.100 --> 00:21:59.490
If we stay together,
we're sitting ducks.

00:21:59.940 --> 00:22:02.900
If the enemy is using missiles, using
armored vehicles will put us at a disadvantage.

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:05.460
We'll split in to two groups
and search for the enemy.

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:06.730
Quick !

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:08.690
They split into
two groups, huh ?

00:22:09.060 --> 00:22:12.360
It's not the wrong way to
deal with an ambush, but...

00:22:12.920 --> 00:22:14.790
It's a chance for us to
take them out one by one.

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:17.280
Two against four would give us a
better chance than two against eight.

00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:18.340
Let's go !

00:22:28.170 --> 00:22:32.930
Space Year 791,
Imperial Year 482...

00:22:32.930 --> 00:22:38.620
The first battle for Reinhard
von Musel and Siegfried Kircheis...

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:44.480
...came to them as a fight for survival rather than for accolades or ambition.

00:22:44.450 --> 00:22:48.100
To be continued

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:58.470
Reinhard:

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:58.470
Horikawa Ryo

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:06.510
Herder:

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:06.510
Miyata Hikaru

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:14.600
Narrator:

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:14.600
Yara Yuusaku

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:26.100
Pour the light into the night sky, a mystic silver curtain

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:24.810
[ Explanations ]

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:24.810
Ending Theme

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:24.810
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:24.810
Written by: Ogura Kei

00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:30.800
The dance of the entire firmament, the mystery of the aurora

00:23:28.110 --> 00:23:33.090
Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:31.100 --> 00:23:35.460
I believe explanations for those will be given some day

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:39.090
Timing:
Todd Perkins

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:46.700
Even the mystery of this life that it is, some day...

